# Implementation Workflow Manager

## Purpose

Coordinates multi-phase implementation with proper Git workflow:
- Auto-creates feature branches for each phase
- Commits work to branch
- Creates PR with description
- Documents what was generated vs manually changed

## When to Use

Apply this workflow when starting a new implementation phase (Phase 2, 3, 4, etc.)

## Workflow Steps

### 1. Branch Creation

Before starting work:

```bash
# Create feature branch
git checkout -b phase-{N}-{short-description}

# Examples:
# git checkout -b phase-2-workflow-nodes
# git checkout -b phase-3-duplicate-detection
# git checkout -b phase-4-testing
```

**Branch naming convention:**
- `phase-{N}-{description}` - Implementation phases
- `fix-{issue}` - Bug fixes
- `docs-{topic}` - Documentation updates

### 2. Implementation

Work on the phase, committing incrementally:

```bash
# Commit logical units of work
git add src/graph/nodes/
git commit -m "Implement preprocess and risk check nodes"

git add src/services/llm_service.py
git commit -m "Add LLM service with structured output validation"
```

**Commit message format:**
```
[verb] [what] [(optional context)]

Examples:
- Add preprocess node with text cleaning
- Implement two-stage duplicate detection
- Fix ValidationError handling in triage node
- Update state schema with secondary_issues field
```

### 3. Push Branch

```bash
# Push feature branch
git push -u origin phase-{N}-{description}
```

### 4. Create PR

```bash
# Using gh CLI
gh pr create \
  --title "Phase {N}: {Title}" \
  --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary
[What this phase implements]

## Changes
- [Change 1]
- [Change 2]
- [Change 3]

## Agent-Generated vs Manual
**Agent generated:**
- [Files/code generated by AI]

**Manually changed:**
- [Files you modified after agent]
- Why: [Reason for changes]

**Didn't trust:**
- [Code you reviewed and fixed]
- Why: [What was wrong]

## Testing
- [ ] Unit tests pass
- [ ] Integration tests pass
- [ ] Manual testing on Set B samples

## Addresses
- Spec requirement: [which requirement from spec.md]
- Exercise requirement: [from 1_candidate_brief.md]

EOF
)"
```

**PR Title Format:**
```
Phase {N}: {Short description}

Examples:
- Phase 2: Core workflow nodes implementation
- Phase 3: Duplicate detection with embeddings
- Phase 4: Testing and validation
```

### 5. Review & Merge

After PR created:

```bash
# Run code auditor
@code-auditor audit phase-{N} implementation

# Run QA tests
@qa-tester test phase-{N}

# If failures, run bug-fixer
@bug-fixer fix [issue]

# When approved, merge
gh pr merge --squash
```

