## Exercise Requirement Compliance

The brief states:
> "Commit your work to the Gitea repo and open at least one PR ‚Äî we want to see the flow end to end"

**Our approach:**
1. Each phase = 1 PR
2. PR description documents agent vs manual work
3. Clear commit history shows development process
4. Review step built in (code-auditor, qa-tester)

## Git Best Practices

### DO:
- ‚úÖ Create feature branch for each phase
- ‚úÖ Commit logical units of work
- ‚úÖ Write clear commit messages
- ‚úÖ Document agent-generated vs manual in PR
- ‚úÖ Test before creating PR

### DON'T:
- ‚ùå Work directly on main
- ‚ùå Create giant commits with "misc changes"
- ‚ùå Skip PR description
- ‚ùå Merge without code review (auditor)
- ‚ùå Push broken code

## Auto-Branch Creation Template

When starting a new phase, use this pattern:

```bash
# 1. Ensure main is up to date
git checkout main
git pull origin main

# 2. Create feature branch
PHASE_NUM=2
PHASE_DESC="workflow-nodes"
git checkout -b "phase-${PHASE_NUM}-${PHASE_DESC}"

# 3. Start work
[implementation happens]

# 4. Commit incrementally
git add [files]
git commit -m "[message]"

# 5. Push and create PR
git push -u origin "phase-${PHASE_NUM}-${PHASE_DESC}"
gh pr create --title "Phase ${PHASE_NUM}: [Title]" --body "[Body]"
```

## Integration with Agents

### Before calling implementation agent:

```bash
# Create branch first
git checkout -b phase-2-workflow-nodes
```

### When agent completes:

```bash
# Review changes
git status
git diff

# Stage and commit
git add .
git commit -m "Phase 2: Implement core workflow nodes

- Add all 10 nodes with error handling
- Configure PostgresSaver checkpointing
- Add conditional routing with type hints
- Implement two-stage duplicate detection"

# Push and PR
git push -u origin phase-2-workflow-nodes
gh pr create --title "Phase 2: Core workflow nodes" --body "[see template]"
```

### After PR created:

```bash
# Audit code
@code-auditor audit implementation

# Test behavior  
@qa-tester run Set B tests

# If issues found
@bug-fixer fix [issue]

# Merge when approved
gh pr merge --squash
```

